Description: CVE-2026-32777 - Fix infinite loop in entityValueProcessor
 libexpat before 2.7.5 allows an infinite loop while parsing DTD content.
 The entityValueProcessor function in xmlparse.c is missing a rejection
 check for XML_TOK_INSTANCE_START tokens, which can cause denial of
 service by exhausting CPU resources. This patch adds the missing check,
 matching the identical pattern already present in entityValueInitProcessor.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/commit/55cda8c7125986e17d7e1825cba413bd94a35d02
Author: Sebastian Pipping <sebastian@pipping.org>
Last-Update: 2026-03-17

--- a/expat/lib/xmlparse.c
+++ b/expat/lib/xmlparse.c
@@ -4021,7 +4021,7 @@
     }
     /* If we get this token, we have the start of what might be a
        normal tag, but not a declaration (i.e. it doesn't begin with
-       "<!").  In a DTD context, that isn't legal.
+       "<!" or "<?").  In a DTD context, that isn't legal.
     */
     else if (tok == XML_TOK_INSTANCE_START) {
       *nextPtr = next;
@@ -4099,6 +4099,15 @@
       /* found end of entity value - can store it now */
       return storeEntityValue(parser, enc, s, end);
     }
+    /* If we get this token, we have the start of what might be a
+       normal tag, but not a declaration (i.e. it doesn't begin with
+       "<!" or "<?").  In a DTD context, that isn't legal.
+    */
+    else if (tok == XML_TOK_INSTANCE_START) {
+      *nextPtr = next;
+      return XML_ERROR_SYNTAX;
+    }
+
     start = next;
   }
 }
Description: CVE-2026-66046 - Fix quadratic runtime in attribute default handling
 A malicious XML document that declares a very large number of default
 attributes for a single element could trigger quadratic (O(n^2)) runtime
 in libexpat's attribute processing. This was caused by a linear scan over
 the per-element `defaultAtts` array in storeAtts() (used to determine
 whether a specified attribute was declared as other than CDATA). For a
 large number of default attributes this linear loop made overall
 processing scale quadratically, enabling a denial-of-service.
 .
 The companion collision-detection scan in defineAttribute() was already
 migrated to a per-ELEMENT_TYPE hash table (`defaultAttsNames`) by the fix
 for CVE-2026-45186 (upstream commit 4cd4eb06), which is already applied to
 this package. That table was used only as a set of attribute names. This
 patch upgrades the existing `defaultAttsNames` table in place from a set
 (storing NAMED) to a dictionary (storing NAME_AND_DEFAULT_ATTRIBUTE, which
 records the index of the backing DEFAULT_ATTRIBUTE entry), and migrates the
 remaining storeAtts() .isCdata lookup to it. Both lookups now run in
 (amortised) constant time, resolving the quadratic runtime. No second hash
 table is introduced; initialisation, population and teardown of
 `defaultAttsNames` (in storeAtts(), defineAttribute(), dtdCopy(), dtdReset()
 and dtdDestroy()) are inherited unchanged from the CVE-2026-45186 fix.
 .
 This backports upstream commit f8f7c4ff (migrate the .isCdata lookup from a
 linear loop to a hash-table lookup), adapted to the 2.2.10 HASH_TABLE API
 and reusing the existing `defaultAttsNames` table rather than the renamed
 `defaultAttForName` of upstream prerequisite 98f5acc1. XML_Bool/XML_TRUE and
 an int-typed nDefaultAtts (cast to size_t at the comparison) are used to
 match the 2.2.10 sources.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/commit/f8f7c4ffd883e3c2c58f0ebb49416a6c1d248738
Bug: https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/security
