Description: CVE-2026-56404 - protect addBinding from signed integer overflow
 The addBinding() function in expat/lib/xmlparse.c accumulates a signed int
 length over the URI without bounds checking, which can wrap (CWE-190) on
 extremely long URIs and lead to subsequent allocation/length errors.
 .
 Backport of upstream commit babfc48090977cbf7be24b2c48f6053dca75c164
 (libexpat 2.8.2, PR #1249) adapted to expat 2.2.10. Only the INT_MAX
 guards on the length accumulator itself are imported; the unrelated
 RFC 3986 namespace-separator validation that ships in the same
 upstream function in 2.8.x is NOT carried over.
 .
 Debian's expat 2.2.10-2+deb11u7 already carries the CVE-2022-25313/
 25314/25315 quilts, which independently added INT_MAX/SIZE_MAX guards
 around the "len + EXPAND_SPARE" REALLOC and MALLOC allocations in this
 same function. Those guards run after "len" has already been
 incremented for the namespace separator, so they do not protect the
 "len++" itself from signed overflow when len == INT_MAX. This patch
 only adds the two guards upstream commit babfc480 introduces around
 the length accumulation (the for-loop and the namespace-separator
 increment) and does not duplicate the allocation-size guards Debian's
 quilt stack already provides.
 .
